"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115136","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115136","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115136.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115136.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"In accessible mode, the EventListenerLineEdit no longer captures input automatically on focus. Instead, users press Enter to start listening, then press the desired key. This allows screen reader users to navigate the UI with Tab/Shift-Tab without those keys being captured as bindings.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs an Orca user, I found that tab/shift-tab got captured by this input and there was no way to escape, or to bind keyboard inputs via the UI. This makes the key entry/binding interface much more usable for me.\r\n\r\nAs an aside, I feel like this should be the *default* behavior--don't automatically capture events unless explicitly activated with Enter/Select. I settled for making the behavior accessible-only, though.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115136/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115136/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}